    "result_text": "All clean. The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the string `membershipTier` with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133), keeping each piece of logic in a single, well-placed unit:\n\n1. **New `MembershipLevel` domain helper** (`model/MembershipLevel.java`) \u2014 a single source of truth for the rule: start at `1`, `+1` when an email is present, `+1` when `namesakeCount == 0`, capped at `3`. Named constants `BASE`/`MAX` document that level 4 is reserved for tenure. This mirrors the existing `CityRegion` helper the mapper already delegates to.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 the `@Mapping` target and derivation method now produce `membershipLevel` (an `int`) by delegating to `MembershipLevel.of(owner)`, replacing the old `membershipTier` GOLD/SILVER/BRONZE method. Since it derives live in the mapper, the value surfaces correctly on both the create response and `GET /api/owners/{id}` (the test reads it back via GET).\n\n3. **`AuditOwnerCreated`** \u2014 the create audit line now records `membershipLevel={}` (via the same helper) instead of just identity fields, satisfying \"anything that recorded the tier \u2026 must record the level instead.\" No duplicated formula \u2014 it reuses `MembershipLevel.of`.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 the generated `OwnerDto` field is now `membershipLevel` (`integer`, min 1 / max 3), removing `membershipTier` from the response.\n\nVerification: `AcceptanceTest.coreNumericLevel` passes (`membershipLevel == 3` for a unique owner with email), full suite is `BUILD SUCCESS`, and the audit log confirms `AUDIT - Owner created: \u2026 membershipLevel=3`.\n\nNote: I left the household-member counting (`CountHouseholdMembers`) in place \u2014 the new level formula no longer uses it, but it's an independent stored attribute and removing it would be out of scope for this change. Let me know if you'd like it pruned.",
